### imageproc (MIT)

`src/services/captcha/drawing.rs` is a derivative work of the `imageproc`
crate, v0.26.2 — the text, Bézier, line, circle and noise routines the
renderer calls, specialised to `RgbImage`. It was vendored because `imageproc`
declares `nalgebra` as a non-optional dependency, with no feature to switch it
off; that pulled `simba`, `paste` (RUSTSEC-2024-0436, unmaintained),
`matrixmultiply`, `num-complex`, `approx`, `safe_arch`, `typenum`, `wide` and
`rawpointer` into the build, plus a second major version of `rand` via
`rand_distr`, none of it reachable from the routines actually used.

- Upstream: https://github.com/image-rs/imageproc
- License: MIT
- Copyright: Copyright (c) 2015 PistonDevelopers

