## Embedded Fonts

### Roboto Bold, subset (SIL OFL 1.1)

`assets/fonts/Roboto-Bold-subset.ttf` is compiled into the CaptchAPI binary
via `include_bytes!` and used to render CAPTCHA glyphs.

It is a **Modified Version** under the SIL Open Font License: Roboto Bold
3.015, subset to the 54 characters CaptchAPI actually renders (8,196 bytes).
It is regenerated by `scripts/subset-font.py`.

- Derived from: Roboto Bold, Version 3.015
- Upstream: https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-classic
- License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
- Copyright: Copyright 2011 The Roboto Project Authors

OFL compliance notes:

- Roboto's copyright statement declares **no Reserved Font Name**. Clause 3
  therefore imposes no renaming obligation on this subset, and the family
  name "Roboto" is retained unchanged.
- The copyright (name ID 0), license (13) and license URL (14) records are
  present in the face; Google's CDN build omits the license records, so the
  subset script restores them explicitly.
- The modification is disclosed in the description record (name ID 10).
- The font remains under the OFL and is not sold separately.

The full license text is distributed alongside the font at
`assets/fonts/LICENSE-Roboto-OFL-1.1.txt`.

Roboto replaces the Monotype Arial that `captcha-rs` v0.5.0 embeds; that font
is proprietary and its embedded license notice forbids redistribution, so it
could not be shipped in CaptchAPI's binaries or container images.

